Subject: [PATCH v9 03/10] jails/instances/lab-mail: Let Dovecot write the list
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: nsosnlpzqvrykposnmmpnxsymltpzpsy
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:05:00 +0000

The hub needs one program that writes the list, so posts, syncs, and
Pat's archiving never race on the maildir. While mbsync writes the
maildir and Dovecot only reads it, as another user, neither can take
on the other's work. With Dovecot as the only writer and mbsync as
one of its IMAP clients, the rest of the hub needs no further change
to who owns the list, and readers see no change.

- vmail owns the maildir. mbsync fetches into Dovecot over IMAP, so
  the fetch job no longer opens up the files it writes.
- Dovecot checks the logins in imap-users against their passwords.
  Every other user name still logs in with any password, and the ACL
  lets it only read.
- The ACL comes only from the global file, and lets mbsync write.
- check covers the new secrets and the maildir's new owner.
- README.org gives the rights, the new secrets, and why the maildir
  must start empty.
